Linearly Balanced Quadruples in Four-Term Arithmetic Progressions

This repository contains a short LaTeX note on positive integer quadruples satisfying

[
ab-cd=a+b+c+d,
]

equivalently,

[
(a-1)(b-1)=(c+1)(d+1).
]

Main result

For a four-term arithmetic progression

[
n,\ n+r,\ n+2r,\ n+3r,
]

all linearly balanced pairings are classified, up to exchanging the two variables within each product:

1. r = 1
[
{a,b}={n+2,n+3},\qquad {c,d}={n,n+1}.
]
2. r = 2
[
{a,b}={n+2,n+6},\qquad {c,d}={n,n+4}.
]
3. r >= 4
[
n=\frac{r(r-3)}2,
]
with
[
{a,b}={n+r,n+2r},\qquad {c,d}={n,n+3r}.
]

There is no positive-integer solution with common difference (r=3).

> Note: In item 2, the displayed values are the specialization of
> ({n+r,n+3r}) and ({n,n+2r}) at (r=2).

